  "details": "I have my own group. Recently, the creator of the map (world) we were in joined our group’s open instance and began issuing warnings, muting people’s microphones, and generally trolling everyone as much as possible. These actions don’t fall under the group’s moderation logs, since they are being performed by the map (world) creator rather than a group moderator, administrator, or owner. I propose prohibiting the map creator from moderating instances that are opened by a group or specific individuals, while allowing them to retain moderation rights for instances that are simply public.",
